## Report

**Root cause (exact)**

`DateTime#isInDST()` in `/luxon/src/datetime.js` (lines 1164–1172) decided DST by comparing the current offset with the offset of two probe dates built with `this.set({ month: 1 })` / `this.set({ month: 5 })`. `set()` keeps the *day of month*, so for a 1974 US date whose day-of-month is ≥ 6, the "January" probe (`Jan <same day>`) lands **inside** the 1974 year-round-DST window (Jan 6 → Oct 27), returning the same offset as the current instant. Result: `isInDST` was `false` for every 1974 date with day ≥ 6 in the DST window (i.e. Jan 6–31 and Oct 26–27, and generally the whole Jan 6–Oct 27 range for days ≥ 6), exactly matching the bug report. There is no hardcoded US DST table in Luxon 1.20 (IANA offsets come from `Intl` via `src/zones/IANAZone.js`), so the hint about `usDst`/`getUSOffset` was a red herring — the bug is the probe date.

**Fix (only file changed: `src/datetime.js`, lines 1168–1171)**

```diff
@@ -1166,7 +1166,8 @@ export default class DateTime {
       return false;
     } else {
       return (
-        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
+        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
+        this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
       );
     }
   }
```

Pinning the January probe to **Jan 1** makes it a genuine standard-time reference even in 1974 (US DST started Jan 6, so Jan 1 is EST). `npx prettier --list-different src/datetime.js` → clean.

**Verification**

- Scratch script in `/tmp/isindst_check.js` (deleted afterwards), run via `@babel/register` against `src/luxon.js`:
  - `1974-01-06T12:00` NY → `true` (was `false`), `1974-01-05T12:00` → `false`, `1974-03-01T12:00` → `true`, `1974-10-27T00:00` → `true` (was `false`), `1974-10-27T12:00` → `false`, `1974-10-28` → `false`, `1973-06-01` → `true`, `1975-06-01` → `true`, `1975-01-15` → `false`, UTC/invalid → `false`.
  - Whole-1974 scan in `America/New_York` at noon, every day: `isInDST` true for exactly Jan 6 → Oct 26, false outside (0 mismatches).
  - Cross-check of `isInDST` against an independent reference (`offset > min offset over the year`) for 13 zones × 8 years (1970/1973/1974/1975/1982/2000/2019/2021), 1248 samples: 0 mismatches.
- `cd /luxon && npx jest test/datetime` → **553 passed, 2 failed** (same 2 before the fix); `npx jest test/datetime/zone.test.js` → 30/30 passed.
- Full suite `npx jest`: **892 passed, 2 failed** after the fix; I also temporarily reverted just my hunk and re-ran the full suite → **892 passed, 2 failed** (identical). The 2 failures are pre-existing and unrelated: `DateTime#toFormat('FFF')/('FFFF')` French-locale expectations (`09:23:54` vs `9:23:54`, ICU/CLDR version difference in this container). No pre-existing test broke; no test file was modified (`git status test/` clean).

**Caveats / notes**

- Instants genuinely in standard time on the transition days (e.g. `1974-01-06T00:00` EST, `1974-10-27T12:00` EST — 1974 transitions happened at 02:00 local) correctly report `false`; only a nonsensical implementation could report `true` for those.
- Other agents are concurrently editing `src/impl/util.js`, `src/interval.js`, `src/duration.js`, `src/impl/conversions.js`, `src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js`; my change is isolated to `src/datetime.js` and I touched nothing else.
